poetry:limerick@claude-fable-5-2.text:
As the kettle hums, nobody's up,
and I hold the new day like a cup;
for the street has no noise,
there's no hurry, no voice,
and the light climbs the wall while I sup.

poetry:limerick@claude-opus-5-5.text:
As the kettle hums, gentle in tone,
I hold dawn like a cup that's on loan;
crows rehearse on the wire
like a quarrelsome choir;
there's no hurry: the light climbs on its own.
